Certainly! Here's an example PHP code that implements an algorithm for calculating the area of any type of polygon, including concave ones, based on its side lengths and interior angles:
```
function polygonArea($sides, $angles) {
    // check if the number of sides and angles match
    if(count($sides) != count($angles)) {
        return false;
    }

    // calculate the sum of interior angles
    $sum = array_sum($angles);

    // check if the sum of interior angles is valid
    if($sum != (count($sides) - 2) * 180) {
        return false;
    }

    // calculate the semi-perimeter
    $s = array_sum($sides) / 2;

    // calculate the area using Heron's formula
    $area = 1;
    for($i = 0; $i < count($sides); $i++) {
        $area *= ($s - $sides[$i]);
    }
    $area = sqrt($area * $s);

    return $area;
}
```
To use this function, simply pass in an array of side lengths and an array of interior angles, like so:
```
$sides = array(5, 6, 7, 8);
$angles = array(90, 90, 90, 90);
$area = polygonArea($sides, $angles);
echo "The area of the polygon is: " . $area;
```
