To get the numerical values of x and y, you can substitute values for one of the variables and solve for the other. For example, if we want to find the value of x when y = 2, we can do:
```
x_val = subs(solx, y, 2);
```
This will give you the value of x when y is 2. Similarly, if we want to find the value of y when x = 3, we can do:
```
y_val = subs(soly, x, 3);
